  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CWGH Promoting SRHR and Gender Justice for Women, Girls &amp; PwD in Mangwe and Bubi Districts by 2025</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The initiative will promote the Sexual and Reproductive Health (SRH) of women, girls, youths, and PWDs through advancing gender justice in Mangwe and Bubi by 2024. The project will address several challenges related to gender inequality, poverty, and SRHR using a three-pronged approach:

Increase awareness of basic health, hygiene, SRHR, and services in the targeted communities
Promote the adoption of safe practices that promote gender equality, challenge harmful gender norms, and address stigma and discrimination at the community level
Create and utilize existing spaces for women, girls, and PWDs to engage with service providers and duty bearers for adoption, budgeting, implementation, and prioritization of gender-just health services at subnational and national levels. The target group will be capacitated to participate in budget consultative meetings at the subnational level so that they raise their issues of concern. Platforms will be provided for participation in pre and post-budget meetings organised by CWGH and other CSOs including Poverty Reduction Trust (PRT)</narrative>
  </description>
